course: dictionary
lesson: 787
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Bedding is one word with three meanings, so the sentence must tell you which one is meant. Read the words around it, then ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «A portable heater must be kept away from curtains and bedding.» The curtains are in the room, so bedding means the sheets and blankets on a bed.
explain: «Hamsters run long distances each night and need a big cage with deep bedding and a big wheel.» A hamster does not sleep on sheets, so bedding here means the straw or wood shavings in its cage.
explain: To check your answer, swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: Bedding is uncountable, so you say some bedding, not a bedding.
fact: «Bedding» can mean the sheets, blankets, duvets, pillows and pillowcases on a bed.
fact: «Bedding» can also mean straw, hay or wood shavings that animals sleep on.
fact: Bedding plants are small flowers planted in a garden bed for one season.
fact: Bedding should be washed regularly, often once a week, because sweat, skin flakes and dust mites collect in it.
exercise: «A portable heater must be kept away from curtains and bedding.» In this sentence, bedding means | Wood for building a fence | *The sheets, blankets and pillows on a bed | Straw for animals to sleep on | Small flowers planted in a garden
exercise: «Hamsters need a big cage with deep bedding.» What is the bedding for? | Keeping the cage warm for the hamster to sleep on | A bed for the owner to sit on | Growing flowers around the cage | *Straw or wood shavings for the hamster to sleep on
exercise: Ella says bedding is only for people's beds. Is she right? | No, bedding is only found in gardens | Yes, only people have bedding | No, bedding is only the pillows on a bed | *No, animals such as rabbits and hamsters need bedding too
test: «Bedding plants brighten flower beds.» In this sentence, what does bedding mean? | *Small flowers planted in a garden for one season | Sheets and blankets on a bed | Wood for a fire | Straw for animals
test: Why is bedding washed hot in «washing bedding hot and airing it keeps them down»? | *To kill and remove dust mites that live in it | To make the bedding grow flowers | To stop the bedding from being used by pets | To turn the bedding into straw
exam: «Wash the bedding once a week.» Which meaning of bedding fits this sentence best? | Small flowers in a garden bed | Hay used to feed a horse | *The sheets, blankets and pillows on a bed | Straw in an animal's cage
